      "message": "\u003e Adapt swap_cgroup_cmpxchg to no longer rely on the global swap cgroup lock,\n\nThat\u0027s unfortunate...\n\n`swap_cgroup_cmpxchg` is also only for v1\u0027s `move_charge_at_immigrate` which has been deprecated since 2022, and was removed a year ago.\n\n`move_charge_at_immigrate` and memcg v1 are dead ends. You need to move off of them.\n\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/20221206171340.139790-4-hannes@cmpxchg.org/\nhttps://lore.kernel.org/all/20241025012304.2473312-1-shakeel.butt@linux.dev/\n\n---\n\nHowever the rest of the patches in this series look like they are worth taking (especially `mm/swap_cgroup: remove global swap cgroup lock`), and `swap_cgroup_cmpxchg` blocks that.\n\nThis conflict *seems* small enough to be manageable but even what\u0027s implemented here looks like it should be retrying the `cmpxchg` if it fails, like `__swap_cgroup_id_xchg` does. I don\u0027t like the idea of maintaining out of tree cgroup v1 code, and especially not any charge moving code.",
